      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "A use case for this could be let's say, you prefer to keep perms to only friends, but want to allow those you trust with perms who aren't in your immediate friend circle without having to friend them. On a per-user basis would fit in as well given the theme of the icon being \"offering a handshake\". Which _maybe_ you don't want to extend a hand to _everyone_ but want to with more who aren't friended with you if you so choose.\nOf course it would still work the same way as the current toggle in which perms would be have to be allowed by both parties for interaction to occur.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
